  "notes": "Official cause_code and category were not provided in FORM-366 FIELDS (marked TBD/provisional); left as-is per rule 4 rather than re-derived from narrative wording, though narrative clearly describes a procedure-adequacy/personnel-performance issue. Reporting-basis citations were garbled/OCR-corrupted in the narrative's block 6 section; inferred standard 10 CFR 50.73(a)(2)(i)(B) and (a)(2)(iv)(A) citations for automatic RPS actuation/reactor trip are typical for this type of event but are best-effort reconstructions from badly OCR-mangled text -- treat with caution. No specific manufacturer, EIIS bracket codes, or component identifiers beyond relay/breaker names were given, so no Manufacturer nodes or eiis_code values were assigned. Feedwater isolation valve erratic indication and one failed intermediate range nuclear instrumentation channel were mentioned as post-trip observations that did not complicate the event; per instructions these were not modeled as separate failure modes in the causal chain since they were not the trip's cause and are noted as inconsequential in the narrative."
